  partName: Right Rear Bolt 2
  description: The Right Rear Bolt 2 is another tiny, complex-shaped component situated
    at the bottom-right-rear of the engine, constructed from Material.001, which
    provides supplementary support and reinforcement to the engine's rear section,
    working in tandem with the Right Rear Bolt to distribute the engine's weight
    and stresses evenly, and its compact design facilitates a secure connection with
    adjacent components. The presence of this bolt underscores the importance of
    redundancy in critical engine components, ensuring that the engine remains stable
    and secure even in the event of component failure. Interestingly, the Right Rear
    Bolt 2 is often subjected to unique stress patterns due to its position near
    the engine's exhaust system, necessitating careful design and testing to ensure
    reliability and durability.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
